
SYNCUP - REAL-TIME FEED APPLICATION  


BEFORE YOU START (Install These First)

Software: Node.js | Download: [https://nodejs.org/](https://nodejs.org/) | Version: v18 or higher  
Software: MongoDB | Download: [https://www.mongodb.com/try/download/community](https://www.mongodb.com/try/download/community) | Version: Latest  
Software: Redis | Download: [https://github.com/microsoftarchive/redis/releases](https://github.com/microsoftarchive/redis/releases) | Version: Redis-x64-3.0.504.msi  


QUICK START (5 Steps)

Step 1: Start MongoDB & Redis (Open Command Prompt as Administrator)  
net start MongoDB  
net start Redis  

Step 2: Open Terminal 1 - Backend  
cd backend  
npm install  
npm run dev  

Step 3: Open Terminal 2 - Frontend  
cd frontend  
npm install  
npm run dev  

Step 4: Open Browser  
Home Page:  http://localhost:3000  
Admin Page: http://localhost:3000/admin  

Step 5: Test the App  
1. Go to Admin page (http://localhost:3000/admin)  
2. Enter Title, Content, Author  
3. Click "Create Feed"  
4. Switch to Home page - feed appears instantly  

WHAT EACH PAGE DOES

Home: http://localhost:3000 → View all feeds (updates automatically)  
Admin: http://localhost:3000/admin → Create new feeds  

HOW IT WORKS

Admin Page → Create Feed → Save to MongoDB → Clear Redis Cache → Send Real-time Update → Home Page Shows Instantly  

